ah, okay. so the issue is that `someObject` hasn't been initialized. you need to create an instance of whatever class `someObject` belongs to before you can call methods on it. something like this should work:

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SomeClass someObject = new SomeClass();
        System.out.println(someObject.someMethod());
    }
}
```

make sure `SomeClass` is the actual class name you're dealing with. that should fix the null pointer exception. ///
